WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.836
Customers 1 and 2 signed up without a referral.

2
00:00:05.836 --> 00:00:10.841
Their referred_by column holds NULL, a marker that means no value: unknown.

3
00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:14.547
Which customers did Asha, customer 1, not refer?

4
00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.938
Of these six, four.

5
00:00:15.938 --> 00:00:20.696
The obvious query keeps rows where referred_by is not equal to 1.

6
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.767
Customer 1: is NULL different from 1?

7
00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:26.634
Nobody knows, so SQL answers unknown.

8
00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:28.493
Not true, and not false.

9
00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:32.695
Any comparison with NULL is unknown, even NULL equals NULL.

10
00:00:32.695 --> 00:00:35.699
Two unknown values might or might not match.

11
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.306
And WHERE keeps a row only when the test is true.

12
00:00:39.306 --> 00:00:40.348
False drops it.

13
00:00:40.348 --> 00:00:41.808
Unknown drops it too.

14
00:00:41.967 --> 00:00:44.787
So the query returns customers 4 and 6.

15
00:00:44.787 --> 00:00:48.764
Customers 1 and 2 vanish, with no error and no warning.

16
00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:52.766
Say what you mean instead: not equal to 1, or IS NULL.

17
00:00:52.766 --> 00:00:58.324
IS NULL is always true or false, never unknown, so customers 1 and 2 come back.

18
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.359
COALESCE does the same job another way.

19
00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:05.831
It swaps a NULL for a value you pick, here 0, and 0 is not 1.

20
00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:08.024
NOT IN hides the same trap.

21
00:01:08.024 --> 00:01:10.383
Which customers referred nobody?

22
00:01:10.383 --> 00:01:15.029
Ask for each customer_id NOT IN the list of referred_by values.

23
00:01:15.029 --> 00:01:17.388
The answer should be 4, 5 and 6.

24
00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:21.104
NOT IN means different from every value in the list.

25
00:01:21.104 --> 00:01:29.335
Customer 4 differs from 1, 2 and 3, but against NULL the answer is unknown, and one unknown makes the whole test unknown.

26
00:01:29.533 --> 00:01:33.050
Customers 1 to 3 are in the list, so they're false.

27
00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:34.360
4 to 6 are unknown.

28
00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.636
The query returns nothing at all.

29
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:42.385
The fix keeps NULL out of the list: add WHERE referred_by IS NOT NULL inside it.

30
00:01:42.385 --> 00:01:44.131
Now 4, 5 and 6 come back.

31
00:01:44.333 --> 00:01:48.223
A comparison with NULL is unknown, and WHERE keeps only true.

32
00:01:48.223 --> 00:01:52.304
At every not equal and every NOT IN, ask which side can be NULL.
